                <pb facs="0212" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv09/pg202"/>

                <head>Appendix D to HD–94</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[<hi rendition="#italic">Telegrams Submitted to the Supreme
                        Council by the British Delegation</hi>]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">1. Telegram from PANAC to the British delegation at the Peace
                    Conference (Nov. 15th, 1919).</p>
                <p>Following has been received from Admiral Goette No. 1112 of Nov. 14th,
                    begins:—Reference your Wireless Signal 1237 of 28th October, steps are being
                    taken for the delivery of the tank steamers, ends.</p>
                <pb facs="0213" n="203" xml:id="pg203"/>
                <p rendition="#flush">2. Telegram from the British Ministry of Shipping to the
                    British delegation at the Peace Conference (Nov. 15th, 1919).</p>
                <p>Message now received by PANAC from Goette that steps are being taken for delivery
                    of tank steamers. Unless Supreme Council decides otherwise management
                    arrangements previously made will be carried out on their arrival at Firth of
                    Forth. So far as Shipping Controller is concerned no compromise in this matter
                    can be considered.</p>
            </div>
